IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa25-communications`

-- coa25-tests-communications.l4: tests for coa25-communications.l4 (ss 1143 to 1148).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section and written down before the run.
-- The calendar used for working days is a TEST fixture: Monday to Friday are working days (the keel's s 1173(1) also
-- excludes Christmas Day, Good Friday and bank holidays, which a caller supplies). 1 January 2026 is a Thursday, so
-- Fri 2 Jan, Sat 3 Jan, Sun 4 Jan, Mon 5 Jan, Tue 6 Jan, Wed 7 Jan, Thu 8 Jan, Fri 9 Jan, Mon 12 Jan, Tue 13 Jan.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` MEANS NOT (`is weekend` d)

-- The same, with Friday 9 January 2026 a bank holiday.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1147 test calendar with Friday 9 January 2026 a holiday` MEANS (NOT (`is weekend` d)) AND NOT (d EQUALS (Date 9 1 2026))

-- A calendar with no working day at all.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1147 test calendar with no working day` MEANS FALSE

-- The penalty that s 1145(5) states: level 3 and one-tenth of level 3.
`s 1145 test penalty level 3 with a tenth` MEANS
    Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                 `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                 `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                 `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                 `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- ---- s 1143(1) (the number of the section or Schedule)
#ASSERT `s 1143(1) the provision is one of the company communications provisions` (`s 1143 a section of the Companies Act 2006` 1144) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1143(1) the provision is one of the company communications provisions` (`s 1143 a section of the Companies Act 2006` 1146) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1143(1) the provision is one of the company communications provisions` (`s 1143 a section of the Companies Act 2006` 1148) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1143(1) the provision is one of the company communications provisions` (`s 1143 a section of the Companies Act 2006` 1143) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- s 1143 itself is not listed
#ASSERT `s 1143(1) the provision is one of the company communications provisions` (`s 1143 a section of the Companies Act 2006` 1149) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1143(1) the provision is one of the company communications provisions` (`s 1143 a Schedule to the Companies Act 2006` 4) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1143(1) the provision is one of the company communications provisions` (`s 1143 a Schedule to the Companies Act 2006` 5) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1143(1) the provision is one of the company communications provisions` (`s 1143 a Schedule to the Companies Act 2006` 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1143(1) the provision is one of the company communications provisions` (`s 1143 a Schedule to the Companies Act 2006` 6) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1143(1) the company communications provisions have effect for the purposes of the provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1143(1) the company communications provisions have effect for the purposes of the provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1143(2) the company communications provisions yield to the other provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1143(2) the company communications provisions yield to the other provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1143(3) the company communications provisions yield to Part 35` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1143(3) the company communications provisions yield to Part 35` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1143(4) the provision is regarded as contrary to the company communications provisions` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (arguments: expressly authorises a form; another reason)
#ASSERT `s 1143(4) the provision is regarded as contrary to the company communications provisions` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "by reason only"
#ASSERT `s 1143(4) the provision is regarded as contrary to the company communications provisions` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1144 (arguments: direction; the Schedule 4 answer; the Schedule 5 answer)
#ASSERT `s 1144 the Schedule that governs the communication` `s 1144 to a company by a person who is not a company` EQUALS `s 1144 Schedule 4`
#ASSERT `s 1144 the Schedule that governs the communication` `s 1144 by a company to a person who is not a company` EQUALS `s 1144 Schedule 5`
#ASSERT `s 1144 the Schedule that governs the communication` `s 1144 by one company to another company` EQUALS `s 1144 Schedule 5` -- (3): Schedule 4 does not apply
#ASSERT `s 1144 the document or information has been sent or supplied` `s 1144 to a company by a person who is not a company` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- only Schedule 4 counts
#ASSERT `s 1144 the document or information has been sent or supplied` `s 1144 to a company by a person who is not a company` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1144 the document or information has been sent or supplied` `s 1144 to a company by a person who is not a company` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1144 the document or information has been sent or supplied` `s 1144 by a company to a person who is not a company` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- only Schedule 5 counts
#ASSERT `s 1144 the document or information has been sent or supplied` `s 1144 by a company to a person who is not a company` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1144 the document or information has been sent or supplied` `s 1144 by a company to a person who is not a company` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1144 the document or information has been sent or supplied` `s 1144 by one company to another company` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1144 the document or information has been sent or supplied` `s 1144 by one company to another company` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- Schedule 4 does not apply, so its answer is ignored

-- ---- s 1145(1) (arguments: the holder; received otherwise than in hard copy form)
#ASSERT `s 1145(1) the person is entitled to require the company to send a hard copy version` `s 1145 a member of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1145(1) the person is entitled to require the company to send a hard copy version` `s 1145 a holder of the company's debentures` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1145(1) the person is entitled to require the company to send a hard copy version` `s 1145 a member of the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- received in hard copy: the "where" fails
#ASSERT `s 1145(1) the person is entitled to require the company to send a hard copy version` `s 1145 another person` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1145(2): "within 21 days of receipt of the request" (1 March 2026: last day 22 March; 20 February 2026: last day 13 March)
#ASSERT `s 1145(2) the last day for sending the hard copy version` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 22 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 1145(2) the last day for sending the hard copy version` (Date 20 2 2026) EQUALS Date 13 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 1145(2) the company sent the hard copy version in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 22 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the 21st day
#ASSERT `s 1145(2) the company sent the hard copy version in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 23 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the 22nd day
#ASSERT `s 1145(2) the company sent the hard copy version in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the day of the request
#ASSERT `s 1145(2) the company sent the hard copy version in time` (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 13 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1145(2) the company sent the hard copy version in time` (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 14 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1145(2) the company sent the hard copy version in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS NOTHING -- sent before the request: silent

-- ---- s 1145(3), the whole section, the offences and the penalty
#ASSERT `s 1145(3) the company may make a charge for providing the hard copy version` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1145(3) the company may make a charge for providing the hard copy version` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1145 the company has complied with this section` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (arguments: the (1) answer; the (2) answer; a charge was made)
#ASSERT `s 1145 the company has complied with this section` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- sent late
#ASSERT `s 1145 the company has complied with this section` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a charge was made
#ASSERT `s 1145 the company has complied with this section` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1145 the company has complied with this section` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- no entitlement, so the duty does not engage
#ASSERT `s 1145 the company has complied with this section` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1145(4) the company commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1145(4) the company commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1145(4) the company commits an offence` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1145(4) an officer of the company commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1145(4) an officer of the company commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1145(4) an officer of the company commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1145(4) an officer of the company commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1145(4) an officer of the company commits an offence` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1145(5) the penalty for an offence under s 1145` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST `s 1145 test penalty level 3 with a tenth`
#ASSERT `s 1145(5) the penalty for an offence under s 1145` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1145(5) the penalty for an offence under s 1145` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1146
#ASSERT `s 1146(1) the section applies to the authentication of the document or information` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1146(1) the section applies to the authentication of the document or information` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1146(2) the hard copy document or information is sufficiently authenticated` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1146(2) the hard copy document or information is sufficiently authenticated` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (arguments: the company specified a manner; identity confirmed in that manner; a statement of identity; no reason to doubt it)
#ASSERT `s 1146(3) the electronic document or information is sufficiently authenticated` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 1146(3) the electronic document or information is sufficiently authenticated` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a manner was specified and not followed; (b) is for "where no such manner has been specified"
#ASSERT `s 1146(3) the electronic document or information is sufficiently authenticated` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 1146(3) the electronic document or information is sufficiently authenticated` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the company has reason to doubt the statement
#ASSERT `s 1146(3) the electronic document or information is sufficiently authenticated` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no statement of identity
#ASSERT `s 1146(4) the section affects the provision of the articles requiring evidence of authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1146(4) the section affects the provision of the articles requiring evidence of authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1146(4) the section affects the provision of the articles requiring evidence of authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1147(5): 48 hours counted over working days only (arguments: the start; the hours; the calendar; the days to search)
#ASSERT `s 1147(5) the instant at which the period of hours ends` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 2 1 2026), 10) 48 `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 6 1 2026), 10) -- Friday 10:00: 14 h on Friday, none on Saturday and Sunday, 24 h on Monday, 10 h on Tuesday
#ASSERT `s 1147(5) the instant at which the period of hours ends` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 5 1 2026), 10) 48 `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 7 1 2026), 10) -- Monday 10:00: 14 h, 24 h, 10 h
#ASSERT `s 1147(5) the instant at which the period of hours ends` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 6 1 2026), 10) 48 `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 8 1 2026), 10) -- Tuesday 10:00 to Thursday 10:00
#ASSERT `s 1147(5) the instant at which the period of hours ends` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 5 1 2026), 0) 48 `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 7 1 2026), 0) -- Monday 00:00 plus 48 hours ends at midnight of Tuesday, which is 00:00 on Wednesday
#ASSERT `s 1147(5) the instant at which the period of hours ends` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 3 1 2026), 12) 48 `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 7 1 2026), 0) -- posted on a Saturday: the Saturday and Sunday do not count
#ASSERT `s 1147(5) the instant at which the period of hours ends` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 8 1 2026), 10) 48 `s 1147 test calendar with Friday 9 January 2026 a holiday` EQUALS JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 13 1 2026), 10) -- Thursday 10:00, Friday a holiday: 14 h Thursday, 24 h Monday, 10 h Tuesday
#ASSERT `s 1147(5) the instant at which the period of hours ends` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 2 1 2026), 10) 48 `s 1147 test calendar with no working day` EQUALS NOTHING -- the hours can never be used up
#ASSERT `s 1147(5) the instant at which the period of hours ends` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 5 1 2026), 10) 4 `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 5 1 2026), 14) -- a short period within one working day

-- ---- s 1147(2), (3), (4) (arguments for (2): sent by post to a UK address; shown properly addressed, prepaid and posted; the instant posted; the calendar)
#ASSERT `s 1147(2) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by post` TRUE TRUE (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 2 1 2026), 10) `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 6 1 2026), 10)
#ASSERT `s 1147(2) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by post` TRUE FALSE (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 2 1 2026), 10) `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS NOTHING -- the company cannot show it was properly addressed, prepaid and posted
#ASSERT `s 1147(2) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by post` FALSE TRUE (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 2 1 2026), 10) `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS NOTHING -- not sent by post to an address in the United Kingdom
#ASSERT `s 1147(3) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by electronic means` TRUE TRUE (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 2 1 2026), 10) `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 6 1 2026), 10)
#ASSERT `s 1147(3) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by electronic means` TRUE FALSE (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 2 1 2026), 10) `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1147(3) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by electronic means` FALSE TRUE (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 2 1 2026), 10) `s 1147 test calendar Monday to Friday` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): the later of when the material was first made available and when notice of it was received
#ASSERT `s 1147(4) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by means of a website` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 5 1 2026), 9) (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 7 1 2026), 8) EQUALS `s 1147 instant` OF (Date 7 1 2026), 8
#ASSERT `s 1147(4) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by means of a website` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 8 1 2026), 9) (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 7 1 2026), 8) EQUALS `s 1147 instant` OF (Date 8 1 2026), 9 -- the material was made available after the notice was received: "if later"
#ASSERT `s 1147(4) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by means of a website` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 5 1 2026), 9) (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 5 1 2026), 14) EQUALS `s 1147 instant` OF (Date 5 1 2026), 14 -- same day, later hour
#ASSERT `s 1147(4) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by means of a website` (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 5 1 2026), 14) (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 5 1 2026), 9) EQUALS `s 1147 instant` OF (Date 5 1 2026), 14
-- the day (PLAN.md section 4.2's DATE)
#ASSERT `s 1147 the day the document is treated as delivered` (JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF (Date 6 1 2026), 10)) EQUALS JUST (Date 6 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 1147 the day the document is treated as delivered` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6) (arguments: the capacity; contrary provision in the articles; in the debenture instrument; in an agreement)
#ASSERT `s 1147(6) the deeming rules yield to the contrary provision` `s 1147 a member` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1147(6) the deeming rules yield to the contrary provision` `s 1147 a member` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a contrary provision of another kind does not count for a member
#ASSERT `s 1147(6) the deeming rules yield to the contrary provision` `s 1147 a holder of the company's debentures` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1147(6) the deeming rules yield to the contrary provision` `s 1147 a holder of the company's debentures` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1147(6) the deeming rules yield to the contrary provision` `s 1147 a person otherwise than in the capacity of a member or debenture holder` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1147(6) the deeming rules yield to the contrary provision` `s 1147 a person otherwise than in the capacity of a member or debenture holder` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1148
#ASSERT `s 1148(1) the thing is an address` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1148(1) the thing is an address` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1148(1) the body is a company` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1148(1) the body is a company` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1148(1) the body is a company` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1148(1) the thing is a document` `s 1148 a summons` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1148(1) the thing is a document` `s 1148 a notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1148(1) the thing is a document` `s 1148 an order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1148(1) the thing is a document` `s 1148 other legal process` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1148(1) the thing is a document` `s 1148 a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1148(1) the thing is a document` `s 1148 any other document` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1148(2) the reference includes the provision, whatever expression is used` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1148(2) the reference includes the provision, whatever expression is used` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1148(3) the reference to sending or supplying by or to a company includes the case` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1148(3) the reference to sending or supplying by or to a company includes the case` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1148(3) the reference to sending or supplying by or to a company includes the case` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1145(2) as a regulative rule, one holder (a member), run with #TRACE. Expected values, decided from the text:
-- sent on the 20th day: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 1145(2) the company must send the hard copy version within 21 days` Member AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "send the document or information in hard copy form" AT 20

-- sent after 21 days (on the 22nd): BREACH BY Company, because the hard copy version was not sent within 21 days.
#TRACE `s 1145(2) the company must send the hard copy version within 21 days` Member AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "send the document or information in hard copy form" AT 22

-- sent to someone else (a debenture holder) and the 21 days run out: the member's request is unmet: BREACH BY Company.
#TRACE `s 1145(2) the company must send the hard copy version within 21 days` Member AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, `Debenture holder`, "send the document or information in hard copy form" AT 5
    (WAITUNTIL 22)
